bin/
obj/
*.user
.vs/
.idea/
artifacts/
# A contributor who compiles Core under Fable in place leaves the compiler's cache behind. No gate here
# does (Phase 217 moved the compile to the consumer that owns a Fable toolchain, and with it the
# `tests/fable-smoke/` and `tests/hash-parity-probe/` output paths this file used to ignore).
fable_modules/
.fable/

# The shared wire-format conformance corpus (Phase 130) is a separate repository, and one of
# the two places the suite looks for it is inside this repository root — which is where CI
# checks it out, and the simplest place for a contributor to clone it. Ignored so that
# cloning it there never makes the tree look dirty.
/wire-format-fixtures/

# Phase 131 — the proof leg (proofs/check.ps1) installs the pinned F* release beside the model and
# keeps its checked-module cache and fresh extraction under obj/; neither is source.
# Since Phase 164 the cache is PER INVOCATION — proofs/obj/cache-<pid>, one per running check.ps1,
# created and removed by the script — so obj/ now holds a varying set of directories rather than a
# fixed two. The prefix below already covers every one of them; this note is here so that nobody
# adds a second, narrower pattern for them, and so that a stray cache-<pid> left by a killed run
# reads as expected rather than as something that escaped the ignore.
proofs/.fstar/
proofs/obj/
